---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base title="Accessibility" description="Accessibility for the UTG website and iOS app. Report barriers to yad3v.dev@gmail.com." path="/accessibility">
  <div class="wrap page-hero">
    <p class="kicker">Access</p>
    <h1>Accessibility</h1>
    <p>We want this site and the UTG app to be usable with keyboards, VoiceOver, and system settings. If something blocks you, tell us.</p>
  </div>
  <article class="wrap legal">
    <h2>This website</h2>
    <p>These pages are static HTML with a single stylesheet. We aim to meet WCAG 2.2 Level AA for this marketing/legal site: text alternatives, visible focus, skip link, sufficient contrast on dark backgrounds, and at least 44px targets on header controls.</p>
    <p>The hero and feature pages use real app screenshots, including Home Screen widgets. Motion is disabled when your system requests reduced motion.</p>
    <h2>The iOS app</h2>
    <p>UTG is SwiftUI on iOS 18+. We intend to respect system accessibility settings where the OS exposes them (VoiceOver labels, Dynamic Type, Reduce Motion, Increase Contrast) as the app evolves.</p>
    <h2>Report a barrier</h2>
    <p>Email <a class="mail" href="mailto:yad3v.dev@gmail.com">yad3v.dev@gmail.com</a> with the page URL or app screen, your device/OS, and what you were trying to do.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
